{
  "//": [
    "Third-party skill sources — someone else's repo of agent skills you want",
    "installed alongside this engine's own workflow skills.",
    "",
    "This file does NOT belong in the engine checkout. Put it beside rules/ in",
    "whatever private content repo this machine points at, and name it in the",
    "machine config:",
    "",
    "    SBW_SKILLS_MANIFEST=~/dev-conventions/skills.json",
    "",
    "The reason is the same one rules/ ships empty here: a public engine that",
    "shipped a curated roster of another person's skills would be shipping an",
    "opinion. The mechanism is the engine's; the roster is yours.",
    "",
    "Then: `make fetch-skills` (preview) / `make fetch-skills YES=1` to clone",
    "each source at its pin, and `make sync-skills` to link them in.",
    "`make doctor` reports a source that is unfetched, sitting at the wrong sha,",
    "or linked without being declared. A '//' key is a comment and is ignored,",
    "so this file is a valid manifest as it stands — copy it and edit in place.",
    "",
    "The all-zero refs below are refused rather than attempted, so a copy you",
    "have not finished editing says so instead of failing later inside git.",
    "",
    "Fields:",
    "  name           required. Becomes the directory under vendor/external/,",
    "                 so it must be a single safe path segment.",
    "  repo           required. Anything `git clone` accepts.",
    "  ref            required, and a full 40-character sha unless you enjoy",
    "                 surprises. An unpinned source means two machines reading",
    "                 this file install different skills on different days.",
    "  allow          required. Per-source allowlist, by skill directory name.",
    "                 There is no 'install everything' — each skill you adopt is",
    "                 charged against the same session budget as your own, and",
    "                 the one roster that was chosen wholesale turned out to want",
    "                 three of six.",
    "  skills_subdir  optional, defaults to 'skills'. Where in that repo the",
    "                 skill directories live.",
    "",
    "A skill of your own with the same name always wins — sync reports the",
    "shadowing rather than silently preferring one."
  ],
  "sources": [
    {
      "name": "example-motion",
      "repo": "https://github.com/example/motion-skills",
      "ref": "0000000000000000000000000000000000000000",
      "allow": ["animate", "review-animations"]
    },
    {
      "name": "example-store-assets",
      "repo": "https://github.com/example/store-screenshots",
      "ref": "0000000000000000000000000000000000000000",
      "skills_subdir": "skills",
      "allow": ["app-store-screenshots"]
    }
  ]
}
